# scripts/provision.env.example — operator/provisioning-time variables for
# scripts/provision-vps.sh and scripts/provision-supabase-stack.sh.
#
# ⚠ Deliberately NOT merged into the repo-root .env.example. That file's own
# header states its scope precisely: "ONLY the secrets the V1 web-app
# container is permitted to hold" — enumerating only that surface's secrets
# IS the security property there. These variables are a different surface
# entirely (host-side, human-run-once, never injected into any container),
# so they get their own example file rather than diluting that one's
# invariant. Both live under a gitignored `.env` at the repo root at runtime
# — the split is about what's DOCUMENTED where, not where the real file goes.
#
# Copy the lines you need into the real, gitignored .env at the repo root.
# Never commit a filled-in copy of this file.

# --- Hetzner (scripts/provision-vps.sh, Phase 1) ---------------------------
# Where: Hetzner Cloud Console -> the project -> Security -> API Tokens ->
# Generate. Verify that path live — the console moves.
# Permission: Read & Write. The script creates servers, primary IPs,
# firewalls, and SSH keys — a read-only token cannot do any of that.
# Lifecycle: needed only while provision-vps.sh runs. Never enters Coolify or
# this repo. Revoke it in the console after the box is up, if you prefer not
# to leave it live.
# Renamed 2026-09-10 from HETZNER_API_KEY — Hetzner calls it an API Token,
# sent as a bearer; this repo's own convention is _TOKEN for bearer tokens
# (see SIMPLEFIN_TOKEN) and _KEY for actual keys. The script does not accept
# the old name as a fallback.
HETZNER_API_TOKEN=<hetzner-api-token>

# --- Coolify admin (scripts/provision-vps.sh, Phase 2 admin bootstrap) -----
# The ONE human-chosen credential in the whole scripted stand-up — everything
# else provision-vps.sh/provision-supabase-stack.sh touch is generated or
# minted on the box. A generated password is secure and unusable; a human
# needs to be able to log into the Coolify dashboard with something they
# picked. COOLIFY_ADMIN_EMAIL / COOLIFY_ADMIN_NAME are non-secret and may
# stay in .env indefinitely. COOLIFY_ADMIN_PASSWORD is a real secret — delete
# the line after the first successful run if you'd rather not leave it
# sitting in a local file (this is no worse than COOLIFY_API_TOKEN, below,
# already living there from the hand-run era of this stand-up). If any of
# the three is missing and the script is run from an interactive terminal,
# it prompts instead of failing — set these only if you want a fully
# unattended run.
COOLIFY_ADMIN_EMAIL=<your-email>
COOLIFY_ADMIN_NAME=<your-name>
COOLIFY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<a-password-you-will-actually-remember>

# --- Coolify API token (read FROM THE BOX by provision-supabase-stack.sh) --
# provision-vps.sh --apply mints this ON THE BOX and writes it to
# /root/.pfin/coolify.env (mode 600) — it is never printed, never returned
# here, and script 2 never reads a local copy. This line only matters for
# the HAND-RUN era of this stand-up (before these scripts existed): if your
# local .env still carries a value here from that period, delete it once
# provision-supabase-stack.sh has run once — the on-box copy is canonical
# from that point on.
COOLIFY_API_TOKEN=<superseded-once-scripted-provisioning-has-run-once>
